            "user": "SamWhited",
            "user_url": "https://api.openstreetmap.org/user/SamWhited",
            "action": "commented",
            "text": "I went and looked, but it seems this has another way to add crossings and I'm not sure what the best way to fix it is though. Having two crossings seems wrong though and gives funny navigation directions.",
            "html": "<p dir=\"auto\">I went and looked, but it seems this has another way to add crossings and I'm not sure what the best way to fix it is though. Having two crossings seems wrong though and gives funny navigation directions.</p>"
          },
          {
            "date": "2023-07-27 11:28:15 UTC",
            "uid": 9637872,
            "user": "gpserror",
            "user_url": "https://api.openstreetmap.org/user/gpserror",
            "action": "commented",
            "text": "seems atlanta road se isn't truly dual carriageway at this segment, is this what you're referring to?",
            "html": "<p dir=\"auto\">seems atlanta road se isn't truly dual carriageway at this segment, is this what you're referring to?</p>"
          },
          {
            "date": "2023-07-27 11:39:18 UTC",
            "uid": 14994176,
            "user": "SamWhited",
            "user_url": "https://api.openstreetmap.org/user/SamWhited",
            "action": "commented",
            "text": "It's not divided, if that's what you mean?\n\nThe problem is that this is a single crossing controlled by a single button on either side, so when navigating by foot the directions tell you to cross the road, then cross the road again as if there's an island in the middle or something for you to stand on, but this seems incorrect and dangerous. Shouldn't this just be a single crossing all the way across both lanes?",
            "html": "<p dir=\"auto\">It's not divided, if that's what you mean?</p>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">The problem is that this is a single crossing controlled by a single button on either side, so when navigating by foot the directions tell you to cross the road, then cross the road again as if there's an island in the middle or something for you to stand on, but this seems incorrect and dangerous. Shouldn't this just be a single crossing all the way across both lanes?</p>"
          },
          {
            "date": "2023-07-27 12:06:53 UTC",
            "uid": 9637872,
            "user": "gpserror",
            "user_url": "https://api.openstreetmap.org/user/gpserror",
            "action": "commented",
            "text": "yeah dual carriageway = \"divided highway\" so if it's merged back to single carriageway at this point to match real life, it would also fix the dual crossing when trying to walk east/west across atlanta road SE?",
            "html": "<p dir=\"auto\">yeah dual carriageway = \"divided highway\" so if it's merged back to single carriageway at this point to match real life, it would also fix the dual crossing when trying to walk east/west across atlanta road SE?</p>"
          },
          {
            "date": "2023-07-27 12:19:52 UTC",
            "uid": 9637872,
            "user": "gpserror",
            "user_url": "https://api.openstreetmap.org/user/gpserror",
            "action": "commented",
            "text": "BTW, it's some work to merge this small section back to single carriageway due to fixing up relations and generating correct turn lanes, not hard but not a quick fix either (probably half hour of work?).  I'm unfortunately lazy right now...\n\n",
            "html": "<p dir=\"auto\">BTW, it's some work to merge this small section back to single carriageway due to fixing up relations and generating correct turn lanes, not hard but not a quick fix either (probably half hour of work?).  I'm unfortunately lazy right now...</p>"
          },
          {
            "date": "2023-07-27 12:50:35 UTC",
